All done — `go vet ./... && go test ./...` exits 0, gofmt clean, all existing tests still pass.

## Changes

**`internal/model/task.go`**
- `Task` gains `Tags []string` (`json:"tags,omitempty"`) and `Due *time.Time` (`json:"due,omitempty"`).
- `Validate()` normalises tags in place (trim, lower-case, de-dup, sort) and rejects any tag not matching `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$` with the new `model.ErrBadTag`; it also snaps `Due` to UTC midnight.
- New helper `NormalizeTag` shared with the query layer.

**`internal/store/store.go`**
- `Version` bumped 1 → 2; version-1 files (missing `tags`/`due` keys) unmarshal fine and are always re-saved as v2.

**`internal/query/query.go`**
- `Options` gains `Tags []string`, `Overdue bool`, `Today time.Time` (set by the CLI from `Env.Now`).
- `--tag` semantics: keep only tasks having ALL wanted tags (normalised before compare).
- `Overdue`: due date strictly before today (UTC date) and never done, even with `IncludeDone`.
- `SortBy "due"`: ascending, no-due last, ties by ID.

**`internal/cli/cli.go` / `format.go`**
- `add`: repeatable `--tag` and `--due YYYY-MM-DD`; bad date/tag → exit 2.
- `edit`: `--tag`, `--untag` (no-op if absent), `--due` / `--due none`; `ErrBadTag` mapped to a usage error like the other validation errors.
- `list`: `--tag` (repeatable), `--overdue`, `--sort due`; combines with `--all`/`--sort id|priority`.
- New `tags` command: `<tag> <count>` per line over open tasks, sorted; usage message updated to mention `tags`.
- `FormatTask` appends ` (due YYYY-MM-DD)` then `[tag1,tag2]`.

**`README.md`** — updated with the new flags and the `tags` command.

**New tests**: `model/tags_test.go` (normalisation, bad tags, due-midnight), `store/version_test.go` (v1 load, v2 round-trip, newer-version rejection), `query/tags_test.go` (tag/overdue/sort-due), `cli/tags_test.go` (add/edit/list flags, usage exit codes, `tags` output, usage message).
